(V)--one of कश्यप's wives and a daughter of दक्ष. Had द्विमूर्धा and sixty other sons;
1: भा. VI. 6. २५; २९-31; वा. ६६. ५५; Vi. I. 5. १२४.
मायाशिता;
2: Br. III. 3. ५६; 6. 1-2; 7. ४६६.
also mother of १०० sons of whom Vipracitti was the chief; mother of the दानवस्; a mother-goddess.
3: M. 6. 1 and १६; १४६. १८; १७१. २९ and ५८; १७९. १९.

--a dharma;
1: वा. २३. १०१.
a शिष्टाचार;
2: Br. II. ३२. ४१.
three kinds of; superior, middling and inferior; the first and last of which are called respectively ज्येष्ठ and कनिष्ठ; the lower and the higher not fit for one's own welfare; the middling is the equal dis- tribution among the deserving; the superior gift leads to मोक्ष and the inferior to one's own welfare;
3: Ib. II. ३२. ५४-56; वा. ५९. ४९-50.
he who per- forms sacrifice by ill-gotten wealth does not attain the fruits thereof; his gifts are not for dharma but only for show; but well-earned money given to right men without expecting fruits, merits Bhoga while Satya leads to heaven;
4: Ib. ६७. २७; ९१. १०६-12; १०४. १४.
the mak- ing of, in a श्राद्ध and the fruits thereof;
5: Br. III. 4. २४; १६. 1.
one of the उपायस् of a king; even Gods are brought under control by gifts; sixteen kinds of; done by काम, अम्बरीष, पृथु, प्रह्लाद and others;
6: M. २२२. 2; २२४. 1-4; २४६. २५-7; २७४ (whole).
the विधि of, enquired by Manu from the Matsya.
7: Ib. 2. २३.
Incumbent on all castes
8: Vi. III. 8. २२.
useless if given to a non- श्रोत्रिय;
9: Ib. V. ३८. ३०.
conditions appropriate to.
